      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\( x \\) given that \\( x^2 = 729 \\) and \\( x \\) is positive, we need to take the square root of both sides of the equation. The square root of a number is a value that, when multiplied by itself, gives the original number.\n\nThe equation \\( x^2 = 729 \\) can be written as:\n\\[ x = \\sqrt{729} \\]\n\nNext, we need to determine the value of \\( \\sqrt{729} \\). We know that \\( 729 \\) is a perfect square, and we can find its square root by recognizing that:\n\\[ 729 = 27^2 \\]\nThis is because:\n\\[ 27 \\times 27 = 729 \\]\n\nTherefore, the square root of 729 is 27. Since \\( x \\) is positive, we have:\n\\[ x = 27 \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{27}\\).",
